# Shell scripts are LF, everywhere, always.
#
# `scripts/push.sh` is the only path that pushes, and on 2026-08-17 windows-latest went red
# with "could not find the end of the SKIP_CHECKS branch" — the branch was exactly where it
# belonged, but git had checked the file out with CRLF and the assertion searched for a
# literal containing `\n`. tests/secret-gate.test.ts now normalises, so that half is fixed
# in the test.
#
# This line is the other half, and it is not about tests: a shell script checked out with
# CRLF does not run at all. `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` makes the kernel look for an interpreter
# literally named `bash\r` and the shell reports `bad interpreter: ... ^M`. Anyone who clones
# this repo on Windows and runs a script under WSL, git-bash or a container gets that, and
# the error names the interpreter rather than the line endings.
#
# Deliberately narrow. A blanket `* text=auto eol=lf` would renormalise every tracked text
# file on checkout, which is a much larger change to make while fixing a red build.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The guard is LF too, and this line has a stranger history than the one above.
#
# `guard/guard.mjs` used to contain a literal NUL byte — a map-key separator written as a raw
# 0x00 rather than an escape. That made GIT CLASSIFY IT AS BINARY, which silently exempted it
# from CRLF conversion on Windows checkouts. Nobody knew that was load-bearing.
#
# Removing the NUL (so the file could be grepped without `-a`) turned it into an ordinary text
# file, Windows started checking it out with CRLF, and four test files that read the guard and
# do exact string matching went red on windows-latest — including the licence public-key
# substitution, which reported "guard.mjs has no public key block at all".
#
# Two fixes, because either alone leaves a trap. The tests now tolerate CRLF; this line stops
# the conversion happening in the first place, which also keeps guard/guard.mjs and
# plugin/guard.mjs byte-identical on every platform — a property tests/plugin-guard-sync.test.ts
# asserts and which CRLF conversion would not have broken today, but would have eventually.
guard/guard.mjs text eol=lf
plugin/guard.mjs text eol=lf
